{"step_index":1272,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:49:49Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:49:49+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:49:49+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/Challenge_e20263a9.lean`\nTotal Lines: 353\nTotal Bytes: 13918\nShowing lines 15 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n15: open GraphCalc\n16: \n17: lemma minUpTo_le {n : ℕ} {p : ℕ → Prop} [DecidablePred p] (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ n) (hp : p k) :\n18:     minUpTo n p ≤ k := by\n19:   unfold minUpTo\n20:   have hmem : k ∈ (Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p := by\n21:     rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\n22:     exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hk, hp⟩\n23:   have hmin := Finset.min_le hmem\n24:   generalize hmin_eq : ((Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p).min = m\n25:   rw [hmin_eq] at hmin\n26:   cases m with\n27:   | top => contradiction\n28:   | coe val =>\n29:     simp only [WithTop.coe_le_coe] at hmin\n30:     exact hmin\n31: \n32: theorem radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n33:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\n34:     GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\n35:   unfold GraphCalc.radius\n36:   have hmem : GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ∈ Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ := by\n37:     apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\n38:     exact Finset.mem_univ v\n39:   obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Finset.min_of_mem hmem\n40:   rw [hb]\n41:   have hle : (Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ).min ≤ ↑(GraphCalc.eccentricity G v) :=\n42:     Finset.min_le hmem\n43:   rw [hb] at hle\n44:   exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp hle\n45: \n46: lemma le_romanDominationNumber {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n47:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ)\n48:     (h : ∀ f : V → Fin 3, GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f → k ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f) :\n49:     k ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G := by\n50:   unfold GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber\n51:   have h_ex : ∃ f : V → Fin 3, GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f := by\n52:     use (fun _ => 2)\n53:     intro v hv\n54:     dsimp at hv\n55:     have h_false : False := by\n56:       revert hv\n57:       decide\n58:     contradiction\n59:   rcases h_ex with ⟨f₀, hf₀⟩\n60:   have h_mem : GraphCalc.romanWeight f₀ ∈ (Finset.univ.filter (GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G)).image GraphCalc.romanWeight := by\n61:     rw [Finset.mem_image]\n62:     exact ⟨f₀, Finset.mem_filter.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_univ f₀, hf₀⟩, rfl⟩\n63:   have h_nonempty : ((Finset.univ.filter (GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G)).image GraphCalc.romanWeight).Nonempty :=\n64:     ⟨GraphCalc.romanWeight f₀, h_mem⟩\n65:   obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := Finset.min_of_nonempty h_nonempty\n66:   rw [hm]\n67:   dsimp\n68:   have hm_in := Finset.mem_of_min hm\n69:   rw [Finset.mem_image] at hm_in\n70:   rcases hm_in with ⟨f_min, hf_min, rfl⟩\n71:   rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hf_min\n72:   exact h f_min hf_min.2\n73: \n74: lemma two_le_romanWeight {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n75:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n76:     (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) (f : V → Fin 3)\n77:     (hf : GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f) :\n78:     2 ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f := by\n79:   unfold GraphCalc.romanWeight\n80:   unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\n81:   unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\n82:   by_contra hc\n83:   have h_le1 : ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≤ 1 := by omega\n84:   have h_no2 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 2 := by\n85:     intro v hv\n86:     have h_mem := Finset.single_le_sum (fun u _ => Nat.zero_le (f u : ℕ)) (Finset.mem_univ v)\n87:     rw [hv] at h_mem\n88:     omega\n89:   have h_no0 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 0 := by\n90:     intro v hv\n91:     have h_f0 : f v = 0 := by\n92:       ext\n93:       exact hv\n94:     obtain ⟨u, _, hu2⟩ := hf v h_f0\n95:     have hu2_nat : (f u : ℕ) = 2 := by\n96:       rw [hu2]\n97:       rfl\n98:     exact h_no2 u hu2_nat\n99:   have h_ge1 : ∀ v : V, 1 ≤ (f v : ℕ) := by\n100:     intro v\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":1273,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"SYSTEM_MESSAGE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:49:49Z","content":"The following is a <SYSTEM_MESSAGE> not actually sent by the user. It is provided by the system as important information to pay attention to.\n\n<SYSTEM_MESSAGE>\n[Message] timestamp=2026-09-11T18:49:46Z sender=0d77a839-cb15-4b7b-9247-e4cbcb2ae788 priority=MESSAGE_PRIORITY_HIGH content=# Swarm Worker 0d77a839 Report: Settle Conjecture e20263a9\n\n## Objective\nSettle `(nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number` in `Challenge_e20263a9.lean`.\n\n## Mathematical Status: TRUE (`prove_e20263a9`)\n1. **Empirical Results**:\n   - Zero counterexamples across all 1,252 connected graphs up to $n=6$.\n   - Zero counterexamples across all non-isomorphic trees up to $n=16$.\n   - Zero counterexamples across hundreds of random graphs ($n \\le 20$) and trees ($n \\le 30$) verified with MILP.\n2. **Analytical Proof**:\n   - For any Roman dominating function $f$:\n     - If $V_2 = \\emptyset$, $\\text{weight}(f) \\ge |V| \\ge \\text{radius}(G) + 1$.\n     - If $|V_2| = 1$ with center $c$, $\\{c\\} \\cup V_0 \\subseteq \\text{ballWithin}(G, 1, c)$ and complement has size $\\le \\text{weight}(f) - 2$. Strict ball expansion yields $\\text{ballWithin}(G, \\text{weight}(f) - 1, c) = V$, so $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{eccentricity}(c) + 1 \\le \\text{weight}(f)$.\n     - For $|V_2| \\ge 2$, centers in a spanning tree are at distance $\\le 3$, yielding $\\text{radius}(G) \\le \\lfloor \\frac{3|V_2|-1}{2} \\rfloor + |V_1| \\le 2|V_2| + |V_1| - 1 = \\text{weight}(f) - 1$.\n\n## Formal Verification Progress in Lean 4\nFormally verified and compiled 22 top-level helper lemmas in `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` and `scratch.lean`:\n1. `minUpTo_le`: Bounding `minUpTo n p` by any satisfying witness $k \\le n$.\n2. `radius_le_eccentricity`: Computable radius bounded by eccentricity of any vertex.\n3. `le_romanDominationNumber`: Dominance bound over all Roman dominating functions.\n4. `two_le_romanWeight`: Roman dominating weight $\\ge 2$ on nontrivial graphs.\n5. `ballWithin_subset_succ` & `ballWithin_subset_add`: Monotonicity of ball expansion.\n6. `ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_add` & `ballWithin_succ_eq_self_implies_univ`: Stagnation analysis.\n7. `card_ballWithin_succ_of_ne_univ` & `ballWithin_univ_or_card_ge`: Strict growth of non-universal balls.\n8. `ballWithin_card_pred_eq_univ` & `eccentricity_le_card_pred`: Eccentricity bounded by $|V| - 1$.\n9. `radius_add_one_le_card`: Fundamental bound $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le |V|$.\n10. `mem_ballWithin_of_walk` & `mem_ballWithin_of_walk_le`: Walk endpoints in `ballWithin`.\n11. `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_forall_walk`: Universal reachability from bounded walks.\n12. `card_ballWithin_add` & `ballWithin_eq_univ_of_card_add`: Multistep expansion lower bound and universal convergence.\n13. `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le`: Bound when $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$.\n14. `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`: Bound $|V| \\le \\text{romanWeight}(f)$ when no 2 is present.\n15. `mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj` & `mem_ballWithin_one_self`: 1-step ball contains center and neighbors.\n\n## Verification\n- `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/antigravity/check.sh Challenge_e20263a9.lean` exits 0 with `LINT: ok` and only standard axioms (`propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`).\n- Created `REPORT.md` and `output_0d77a839.md`.\n- Workspace: `/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9`\n</SYSTEM_MESSAGE>"}
